WHAT THIS MEANS
====================================================================================================
  1. C0 validates the transcription: all 13 rows are self-consistent with the
     paper's own definition of a constacyclic generator, under every conjugate
     naming of omega.  The table data was read correctly.

  2. C2 holds in all 13 rows.  Every printed code dimension is the sum of the
     COMPONENT dimensions with no factor |S(nu)| = 2.  The defect found in
     Examples 2-3 is uniform across the whole table, not local to them.

  3. In 8 of 13 rows the true dimension 2k exceeds the printed length 2n,
     so those printed Gray images cannot exist as subspaces of F_q^{2n}.
     In 3 more rows (2, 4, 8) 2k equals 2n, so the image would be the
     whole space and d = 1, contradicting the printed d.
     Only rows 5 and 9 escape the dimension argument entirely.

  4. C6 and C7 hold in all 13 rows: the EAQECC arithmetic is internally
     consistent.  The error is upstream, in the inputs -- a confirmation of
     the diagnosis, not a new defect.

  LIMITATION. Dimensional/arithmetic audit only.  The printed minimum
  distances were NOT verified, and corrected parameters were NOT computed
  (FINAL_F11_EVIDENCE_DOSSIER.md section 4.3, item c1).
